<title>USA: AEP Cook 2 Mich. nuclear unit at 60 pct.</title>
<headline>AEP Cook 2 Mich. nuclear unit at 60 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Electric Power Co's 1,090 megawatt (MW) Cook 2 nuclear unit was operating at 60 percent power Wednesday morning following an unexpected outage earlier this week, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said.</p>
<p>The unit, in Bridgman, Mich., tripped off line last Friday after a feed regulator valve controller failed.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with a rated capacity of 1,020 MW, was still shut for a refueling outage, expected to last until about April 14.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
</text>
